  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes `typecheck`. I could not render it or run `vite build`, so the look (light intensities, spark visibility, bloom) is untested.\n\n- **Crystals:** seven hexagonal prisms with pointed tops, built as one custom mesh with `geometry.define`. They differ in height, radius and tilt. Every face is flat-shaded with its own normal and its own vertex colour.\n- **Rotation and base:** the cluster turns slowly (0.35 rad/s) on a pedestal inside a ground disc, with an emissive ring around the pedestal edge. The pedestal and ground stay still.\n- **Sparks:** two additive particle emitters, one cool white-blue and one warm, rise gently from the ground disc with noise drift and fading.\n- **Look:** near-black background with fog, and a dim fill light. Cyan and magenta point lights sit behind and to the sides as rim lights. Bloom is on, and the rotation and particles change every frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and one animation frame.\n\n",
